.TH QUANT_UTILS 1 "2026-06-29" "Symoneural" "Symoneural Helper Utilities"
.SH NAME
quant_utils \- quantisation preset helper for GGUF models
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python helpers/python/quant_utils.py list
.PP
.B python helpers/python/quant_utils.py info
.I PRESET
.PP
.B python helpers/python/quant_utils.py estimate
.I PARAMS
.I PRESET
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quant_utils.py
manages named quantisation presets for llama.cpp and stable-diffusion.cpp,
lists available presets, displays preset details, and estimates on-disk model
size in GB for a given parameter count and preset.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Print all available presets with bits-per-weight and description.
.TP
.B info \fIPRESET\fR
Print full details for
.I PRESET
as JSON, including the llama.cpp
.B \-\-outtype
flag value and suitable-for tags.
.TP
.B estimate \fIPARAMS\fR \fIPRESET\fR
Estimate on-disk size in GB.
.I PARAMS
is the number of parameters (e.g.
.B 7e9
for a 7B model).
.SH AVAILABLE PRESETS
.PP
.BR fp32 ", " fp16 ", " bf16
(full-precision),
.BR q8_0
(8-bit near-lossless),
.BR q5_k_s ", " q5_k_m
(5-bit K-quant),
.BR q4_k_s ", " q4_k_m
(4-bit K-quant — recommended),
.BR q4_0 ", " q4_1
(legacy 4-bit),
.BR q3_k_s ", " q3_k_m
(3-bit K-quant),
.B q2_k
(2-bit extreme).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
List all presets:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/quant_utils.py list
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show preset details:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/quant_utils.py info q4_k_m
.EE
.RE
.PP
Estimate a 7B model size at Q4_K_M:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/quant_utils.py estimate 7e9 q4_k_m
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gguf_inspect (1),
.BR diffusion_convert (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Symoneural contributors.
